OL,3,GNEWSARacehorse trainer's fire death
OL,4,Aaccidental - inquest
OL,5,
OL,6,FA car fire which killed a racehorse
OL,7,Ftrainer was likely started by "smoking
OL,8,Fmaterial coming into contact with
OL,9,Fignitable material" in the vehicle, an
OL,10,Finquest has heard.
OL,12,FHugh Mulryan was found dead in the
OL,13,Fdriver's seat of his vehicle at the
OL,14,Fside of Marishes Lane near Malton,
OL,15,FNorth Yorkshire, at about 04:30 BST on
OL,16,F16 June 2025.
OL,18,FOriginally from Galway, Ireland, the
OL,19,F25-year-old had arrived in England two
OL,20,Fdays earlier and was due to begin a job
OL,21,Fas an assistant trainer on the morning
OL,22,Fof his death.
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
